===Motivation===

[[bip-0369.mediawiki|BIP 369]] introduces SPHINCS+ signature verification in Tapscript via the Taproot annex. [[bip-0368.mediawiki|BIP 368]] requires internal key disclosure in the annex for key-path spends. Both BIPs introduce annex data that must be carried through the signing pipeline and included in the final witness.

For the recommended "full insurance" construction (separate Schnorr and SPHINCS+ tapleaves), the signing workflow is straightforward: SPHINCS+-only tapleaves do not contain Schnorr checks, so SPHINCS+ signing is independent and single-round.

For hybrid scripts (both Schnorr and SPHINCS+ checks in the same tapleaf), a two-round signing workflow is required because the [[bip-0342.mediawiki|BIP 342]] Schnorr sighash includes <code>sha_annex</code>, which depends on the SPHINCS+ signatures in the annex. This ordering constraint cannot be relaxed without breaking soft-fork compatibility with non-upgraded nodes (which enforce BIP 342 Schnorr validation including <code>sha_annex</code>).

Without standardized PSBT fields, carrying annex data and SPHINCS+ signatures through the PSBT pipeline requires ad-hoc mechanisms. This BIP provides the standard fields.

==Specification==

===New input field types===

The following input field types are added to the PSBT input map:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Name !! <keytype> !! <keydata> !! <keydata> description !! <valuedata> !! <valuedata> description
|-
| SPHINCS+ Tapleaf Public Key || <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_SPHINCS_PUB = 0x1d</code> || <code><32-byte xonly pubkey> <32-byte leaf_hash></code> || The BIP 340 x-only public key used to identify the signing key for the tapleaf, followed by the tapleaf hash. || <code><32-byte sphincs pubkey></code> || The 32-byte SPHINCS+ public key that appears in the tapleaf script as the argument to <code>OP_CHECKSPHINCSVERIFY</code>.
|-
| SPHINCS+ Tapleaf Signature || <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_SPHINCS_SIG = 0x1e</code> || <code><32-byte xonly pubkey> <32-byte leaf_hash></code> || The BIP 340 x-only public key used to identify the signing key for the tapleaf, followed by the tapleaf hash. || <code><4080-byte signature></code> || A 4080-byte SPHINCS+ signature over the [[bip-0369.mediawiki|BIP 369]] sighash (the [[bip-0342.mediawiki|BIP 342]] Tapscript sighash with <code>sha_annex</code> omitted and <code>spend_type = 0x03</code>).
|-
| Taproot Annex || <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_ANNEX = 0x1f</code> || (none) || No key data. || <code><annex bytes></code> || The assembled annex including the <code>0x50</code> prefix. Contains either [[bip-0368.mediawiki|BIP 368]] type <code>0x02</code> data (internal key disclosure for key-path spends) or [[bip-0369.mediawiki|BIP 369]] type <code>0x04</code> data (SPHINCS+ signatures for script-path spends). The two types are mutually exclusive per input: a spend is either key-path or script-path, never both.
|}

===New output field types===

The following output field type is added to the PSBT output map:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Name !! <keytype> !! <keydata> !! <keydata> description !! <valuedata> !! <valuedata> description
|-
| SPHINCS+ Tapleaf Public Key || <code>PSBT_OUT_TAP_SPHINCS_PUB = 0x09</code> || <code><32-byte xonly pubkey> <32-byte leaf_hash></code> || The BIP 340 x-only public key used to identify the tapleaf, followed by the tapleaf hash. || <code><32-byte sphincs pubkey></code> || The 32-byte SPHINCS+ public key in an output's tapleaf. Used by wallets to identify outputs that contain SPHINCS+ tapleaves (e.g., for change detection).
|}

===Type byte assignments===

Input field type values are chosen to follow the last assigned Taproot input field type in [[bip-0371.mediawiki|BIP 371]] (<code>PSBT_IN_TAP_MERKLE_ROOT = 0x18</code>), with space for intermediate assignments:

* <code>0x1d</code> — <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_SPHINCS_PUB</code>
* <code>0x1e</code> — <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_SPHINCS_SIG</code>
* <code>0x1f</code> — <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_ANNEX</code>

Output field type values follow the last assigned Taproot output field type (<code>PSBT_OUT_TAP_BIP32_DERIVATION = 0x07</code>):

* <code>0x09</code> — <code>PSBT_OUT_TAP_SPHINCS_PUB</code>

These type byte values follow sequentially after existing PSBT field type assignments (including [[bip-0373.mediawiki|BIP 373]] MuSig2 fields) to avoid conflicts.

===Signature ordering in the annex===

When multiple <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_SPHINCS_SIG</code> entries exist for the same input (e.g., a tapleaf with multiple <code>OP_CHECKSPHINCSVERIFY</code> opcodes), their signatures must be ordered in the annex to match the '''byte-offset order''' of the corresponding <code>OP_CHECKSPHINCSVERIFY</code> opcodes in the tapleaf script.

This matches the [[bip-0369.mediawiki|BIP 369]] annex cursor semantics: the cursor advances on each ''executed'' <code>OP_CHECKSPHINCSVERIFY</code>, consuming signatures sequentially from the annex in script execution order.

==Signing Workflow==

This section describes how the [[bip-0174.mediawiki|BIP 174]] roles interact when processing a PSBT that contains SPHINCS+ data. The workflow differs depending on the tapleaf construction.

===Hybrid tapleaf with key-path (recommended, two-round for emergency spending)===

The recommended construction uses the Schnorr key as internal key with a single hybrid tapleaf:

<source>
Internal key: <schnorr_pk>   (key-path for normal spending)
Leaf A: <sphincs_pk> OP_CHECKSPHINCSVERIFY OP_DROP <schnorr_pk> OP_CHECKSIG
</source>

In this construction:
* '''Normal spending (key-path):''' standard Schnorr signing per [[bip-0371.mediawiki|BIP 371]]. No annex is needed before activation of [[bip-0368.mediawiki|BIP 368]]; afterward the annex is deterministic type <code>0x02</code> data. '''Single-round.'''
* '''Emergency spending (hybrid leaf):''' requires two-round signing because the [[bip-0342.mediawiki|BIP 342]] Schnorr sighash includes <code>sha_annex</code>, which depends on the SPHINCS+ signatures in the annex. SPHINCS+ signatures must be produced first, then Schnorr. '''Two-round.'''

The two-round complexity only affects the emergency spending path. Normal key-path spending is single-round and maximally efficient (~64 bytes).

===NUMS + hybrid emergency leaf (alternative)===

For users requiring unconditional key-path protection, the NUMS construction disables key-path spending:

<source>
Internal key: H (NUMS)
Leaf A: <schnorr_pk> OP_CHECKSIGVERIFY 1                                        (normal spending)
Leaf B: <sphincs_pk> OP_CHECKSPHINCSVERIFY OP_DROP <schnorr_pk> OP_CHECKSIG      (quantum emergency)
</source>

In this construction:
* '''Spending via Leaf A''' (normal): Schnorr script-path signing. '''Single-round.'''
* '''Spending via Leaf B''' (emergency): hybrid signing (SPHINCS+ then Schnorr). '''Two-round.'''

Normal spending costs ~130 bytes (script-path) instead of ~64 bytes (key-path). Both leaves require a valid Schnorr signature and are safe pre-activation.

===Role descriptions===

====Creator====

Creates the PSBT as usual per [[bip-0174.mediawiki|BIP 174]]. No changes.

====Updater====

The Updater adds SPHINCS+ metadata to inputs and outputs:

# For each input spending a UTXO with a SPHINCS+ tapleaf:
#* Add <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_SPHINCS_PUB</code> with the SPHINCS+ public key and the corresponding <code>(xonly_pubkey, leaf_hash)</code> key data.
#* Add the standard [[bip-0371.mediawiki|BIP 371]] Taproot fields (<code>PSBT_IN_TAP_LEAF_SCRIPT</code>, <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_INTERNAL_KEY</code>, <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_MERKLE_ROOT</code>, <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_BIP32_DERIVATION</code>) as usual.
# For each output with a SPHINCS+ tapleaf (e.g., change outputs):
#* Add <code>PSBT_OUT_TAP_SPHINCS_PUB</code> with the SPHINCS+ public key for the output's tapleaf.

====Signer (SPHINCS+)====

The SPHINCS+ signer processes each input:

# Check for <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_SPHINCS_PUB</code>. If absent, skip (not a SPHINCS+ input).
# Determine the SPHINCS+ tapleaf to sign (using the leaf hash from the key data).
# Compute the [[bip-0369.mediawiki|BIP 369]] sighash: the standard [[bip-0342.mediawiki|BIP 342]] Tapscript sighash with <code>sha_annex</code> '''omitted''' and <code>spend_type = 0x03</code>. Only <code>SIGHASH_DEFAULT</code> (0x00) is supported.
# Produce a 4080-byte SPHINCS+ signature using the wallet's SPHINCS+ secret key.
# Add <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_SPHINCS_SIG</code> with the signature and the <code>(xonly_pubkey, leaf_hash)</code> key data.

For '''separate tapleaf''' constructions (SPHINCS+-only leaf), no further signing rounds are needed. The Combiner can assemble the annex and the Finalizer can produce the witness immediately.

For '''hybrid tapleaf''' constructions, the Schnorr signature cannot be produced until the annex is assembled (see Signer Round 2 below).

====Combiner====

The Combiner collects signatures and assembles the annex:

# Merge <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_SPHINCS_SIG</code> fields from multiple signers if applicable.
# For inputs with SPHINCS+ signatures, assemble the [[bip-0369.mediawiki|BIP 369]] annex:
#* <code>0x50 || 0x04 || compact_size(N) || sig_1 || sig_2 || ... || sig_N</code>
#* <code>N</code> is the number of SPHINCS+ signatures for the input.
#* Signatures are ordered by byte-offset of their corresponding <code>OP_CHECKSPHINCSVERIFY</code> in the tapleaf script.
# For key-path inputs requiring [[bip-0368.mediawiki|BIP 368]] annex:
#* Assemble the annex from <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_INTERNAL_KEY</code> and <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_MERKLE_ROOT</code>:
#* <code>0x50 || 0x02 || P</code> (34 bytes, no script tree) or <code>0x50 || 0x02 || P || merkle_root</code> (66 bytes, with script tree).
# Store the assembled annex in <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_ANNEX</code>.

The Combiner '''does not''' validate the annex format against consensus rules. It assembles the data from the available fields. Consensus validation occurs when the final transaction is broadcast.

====Signer (Schnorr, Round 2 — hybrid tapleaf only)====

For hybrid tapleaf constructions where Schnorr and SPHINCS+ checks coexist in the same script, the Schnorr signer requires the assembled annex:

# Read <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_ANNEX</code> to obtain the annex bytes.
# Compute the standard [[bip-0342.mediawiki|BIP 342]] Tapscript sighash, which includes <code>sha_annex</code> (the SHA-256 hash of the annex). This commits to the exact annex contents, including all SPHINCS+ signatures.
# Produce the Schnorr signature and add it as <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_SCRIPT_SIG</code> per [[bip-0371.mediawiki|BIP 371]].

For '''key-path spends''' with the Taproot key-path hardening draft annex, the annex is deterministic (derived from the internal key and optional merkle root). The Schnorr signer can compute <code>sha_annex</code> directly and sign in a single round. Add the Schnorr signature as <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_KEY_SIG</code>.

For '''separate tapleaf''' constructions (SPHINCS+-only leaf), this round is not needed — there is no Schnorr check in the SPHINCS+ leaf.

====Finalizer====

The Finalizer assembles the final witness from PSBT fields. The annex, if present, is always the last witness element.

=====Key-path spend (the Taproot key-path hardening draft)=====

<source>
witness: [schnorr_sig] [annex]
</source>

Where <code>annex</code> is the <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_ANNEX</code> value (34 or 66 bytes, type <code>0x02</code>).

=====Script-path spend (hybrid leaf)=====

<source>
witness: [schnorr_sig] [script] [control_block] [annex]
</source>

Where <code>schnorr_sig</code> satisfies <code>OP_CHECKSIG</code> in the hybrid script. The SPHINCS+ public key and Schnorr public key are data pushes '''inside the script''', not separate witness elements. The SPHINCS+ signature is carried in the annex, not on the witness stack.

=====Pseudocode=====

<source>
def FinalizeTaprootInput(psbt_input):
    annex = psbt_input.get(PSBT_IN_TAP_ANNEX)

    if is_keypath_spend(psbt_input):
        sig = psbt_input[PSBT_IN_TAP_KEY_SIG]
        if annex:
            witness = [sig, annex]
        else:
            witness = [sig]

    elif is_scriptpath_spend(psbt_input):
        (script, control_block) = select_tapleaf(psbt_input)
        script_witness = build_script_witness(psbt_input, script)
        if annex:
            witness = script_witness + [script, control_block, annex]
        else:
            witness = script_witness + [script, control_block]

    return witness
</source>

==Backward Compatibility==

Participants that do not understand the new field types will ignore them per [[bip-0174.mediawiki|BIP 174]] §Unknown Fields. This means:

* '''Non-SPHINCS+ signers''' can still produce Schnorr signatures if the annex has already been assembled by a Combiner (the <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_ANNEX</code> field provides the annex bytes needed to compute <code>sha_annex</code>).
* '''Legacy Combiners''' will pass through unknown fields without modification, preserving SPHINCS+ data for participants that understand it.
* '''Legacy Finalizers''' that do not recognize <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_ANNEX</code> will produce witnesses without the annex. Post-activation, this produces an invalid transaction ([[bip-0368.mediawiki|BIP 368]] requires the annex for key-path spends; [[bip-0369.mediawiki|BIP 369]] requires it for SPHINCS+ script-path spends). Wallets using these BIPs must use a Finalizer that understands the annex field.

==Security Considerations==

===Signing order (hybrid tapleaf only)===

The two-round signing order is required only for hybrid tapleaf constructions where both Schnorr and SPHINCS+ checks coexist in the same script. The [[bip-0369.mediawiki|BIP 369]] SPHINCS+ sighash omits <code>sha_annex</code> to break a circular dependency; the [[bip-0342.mediawiki|BIP 342]] Schnorr sighash includes <code>sha_annex</code> to commit to the annex contents.

This ordering constraint is imposed by [[bip-0342.mediawiki|BIP 342]] Schnorr sighash rules and cannot be relaxed without breaking soft-fork compatibility. Non-upgraded nodes enforce BIP 342 Schnorr validation (including <code>sha_annex</code>) when evaluating the <code>OP_CHECKSIGVERIFY</code> in a hybrid script.

For the recommended separate-tapleaf construction, this constraint does not apply — SPHINCS+-only tapleaves contain no Schnorr checks, so there is no ordering dependency.

===Annex malleability===

Once <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_ANNEX</code> is set, modifying it invalidates any Schnorr signature that was computed using <code>sha_annex</code>. The presence of both <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_ANNEX</code> and a Schnorr signature (<code>PSBT_IN_TAP_KEY_SIG</code> or <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_SCRIPT_SIG</code>) in the same input implies that the Schnorr signature commits to the current annex contents. Modifying the annex after Schnorr signing produces an invalid transaction.

===PSBT as transport, not validator===

The fields defined in this BIP carry data through the PSBT pipeline. They do '''not''' enforce consensus rules. Specifically:

* The PSBT layer does not validate annex format (type bytes, signature counts, strict length checks).
* The PSBT layer does not enforce signing order.
* The PSBT layer does not verify that SPHINCS+ signatures are valid.

Consensus validation occurs when the finalized transaction is broadcast and included in a block. This separation of concerns matches the existing PSBT design: [[bip-0371.mediawiki|BIP 371]] carries Taproot data without validating Schnorr signatures or script semantics.

===SPHINCS+ signature size===

Each <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_SPHINCS_SIG</code> value is exactly 4080 bytes. PSBT processors should validate this size on deserialization. A PSBT with multiple SPHINCS+ inputs may be significantly larger than a typical Taproot PSBT. Implementations should ensure that PSBT size limits (if any) account for the ~4 KB per SPHINCS+ signature.

===Replay and reuse===

SPHINCS+ signatures are bound to a specific sighash (transaction, input index, tapleaf). A signature produced for one input cannot be replayed against another. The same SPHINCS+ key may appear in multiple inputs of the same transaction; each requires an independent signature over its input-specific sighash.

===Annex type exclusivity===

The annex types defined in [[bip-0368.mediawiki|BIP 368]] (type <code>0x02</code>, key-path) and [[bip-0369.mediawiki|BIP 369]] (type <code>0x04</code>, script-path) are mutually exclusive per input. A Taproot spend is either key-path or script-path, never both. A PSBT input will contain at most one <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_ANNEX</code> value, with either type <code>0x02</code> or type <code>0x04</code> data.

==Test Vectors==

Planned test vectors for this draft include:

* '''SPHINCS+-only script-path spend''' (separate tapleaf, single-round): complete PSBT round-trip from Creator through Finalizer, with serialized PSBT bytes at each stage.
* '''Hybrid Schnorr + SPHINCS+ spend''' (hybrid tapleaf, two-round): demonstrating SPHINCS+ signing, Combiner annex assembly, and Schnorr Round 2.
* '''Key-path spend with the Taproot key-path hardening draft annex''': PSBT with <code>PSBT_IN_TAP_ANNEX</code> containing type <code>0x02</code> internal key disclosure.
* '''Multi-input transaction''': PSBT with both SPHINCS+ and non-SPHINCS+ inputs, showing selective field population.
* '''Serialization''': individual field type/key/value encodings for each new field type.

==Reference Implementation==

A reference implementation will be provided alongside the [[bip-0369.mediawiki|BIP 369]] wallet support implementation on the Bitcoin Core <code>quantroot</code> branch.
